;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "A Mind for Numbers - How to Excel at Math and Science"
 :source "A Mind for Numbers - How to Excel at Math and Science.pdf"
 :page 13
 :exercises "A drop cap opening its chapter.  The oversized T arrives as its own
record, emitted before its paragraph while its baseline sits level
with the second body line - a backward baseline step that must read
as typesetting, not as a scattered column run for the zone repair to
reassemble.  Capturing this page caught exactly that regression: the
cap landed beside the second line as `T understand'.  The cap rejoins
its word without a space (This book), the paragraph carries past the
inset first lines back to the column margin, and the ragged-right
prose of this book must not shatter at its short lines."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
